---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Motorola Solutions / Vigilant | Providers | NoRec.US" description="ALPR cameras, vehicle-location analytics, body/in-car video, evidence and public-safety communications systems." active="surveillance">
<main class="page_shell provider_detail">
  <header class="article_header provider_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">PROVIDER / PLATFORM</p>
    <h1>Motorola Solutions / Vigilant</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">ALPR cameras, vehicle-location analytics, body/in-car video, evidence and public-safety communications systems.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="provider_scope_notice">
    <span class="status_label">EVIDENCE SCOPE</span>
    <p><strong>Vendor capability</strong> describes the provider’s published product features. <strong>Illinois deployment</strong> is listed only when supported by Illinois records or a clearly labeled secondary source.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">ILLINOIS CONNECTION</p>
    <h2>Documented Illinois relationships</h2>
    <div class="provider_evidence_grid">
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Illinois State Police ALPR</h3><p>ISP identifies Motorola Solutions as the primary vendor for its statewide ALPR project.</p></article>
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Forest Park</h3><p>A 2025 Illinois Secretary of State audit identified Motorola ALPR technology in the Forest Park Police Department context.</p></article>
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Illinois State Police video</h3><p>State procurement records document Motorola body-worn and in-car camera systems.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRODUCT / PLATFORM CAPABILITY</p>
    <h2>Published product capabilities</h2>
    <div class="provider_capability_grid">
      <article><h3>Vigilant VehicleManager</h3><p>Motorola describes VehicleManager as LPR analytics software for searching vehicle-location history, hot lists, alerts, and connections between vehicles and locations.</p></article>
      <article><h3>L5F / L6Q / L5M</h3><p>Motorola markets fixed, quick-deploy, and mobile LPR camera systems.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Vehicle attribute search</h3><p>Current product material describes year/make/model filtering and natural-language vehicle-description searches in VehicleManager.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Data-network access</h3><p>Motorola advertises access to detections beyond an agency's own cameras and agency-managed data sharing.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / GOVERNANCE QUESTIONS</p>
    <h2>Privacy and governance</h2>
    <div class="provider_questions">
      <details><summary>Retention</summary><p>Motorola's product materials describe configurable retention settings rather than one universal retention period.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Sharing</summary><p>VehicleManager materials describe agency-managed data sharing and access.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Integrations</summary><p>Motorola describes third-party LPR integration into VehicleManager.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Scale</summary><p>Vendor material advertises access to billions of detections; a particular Illinois agency's accessible dataset must still be proven from agency/vendor records.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="official_product_links">
    <p class="eyebrow">OFFICIAL PRODUCT INFORMATION</p>
    <h2>Vendor documentation</h2>
    <p>Vendor pages describe current products and features. Illinois deployment claims remain tied to Illinois-specific evidence.</p>
    <ul class="provider_source_list">
      <li><a href="https://www.motorolasolutions.com/en_xl/video-security-access-control/license-plate-recognition-camera-systems/vigilant-vehiclemanager-lpr-analytics-software.html" rel="external">Vigilant VehicleManager</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.motorolasolutions.com/en_us/video-security-access-control/license-plate-recognition-camera-systems.html" rel="external">Motorola video security / LPR</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE REFERENCES</p>
    <h2>Illinois records and supporting sources</h2>
    <ul class="provider_source_list">
      <li><a href="https://www.motorolasolutions.com/content/dam/msi/docs/msi-standards_terms-conditions/vigilant-addendum.pdf">Motorola Vigilant contractual addendum</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://isp.illinois.gov/CriminalInvestigations/TransparencyPage">Illinois State Police ALPR transparency page</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.ilsos.gov/news/2025/september-5-2025-giannoulias-audit-uncovers-forest-park-police-department-sharing-license-plate-reader-data.html">Illinois Secretary of State — Forest Park / Motorola audit</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="hero_actions">
    <a class="button button_dark" href="/surveillance/">Back to Surveillance</a>
    <a class="button button_light" href="/sources/">Source Library</a>
  </div>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
